<p><span style=3D"font-size:32px"><strong>What is EO/IR?</strong></span></p=
>

<p>=E2=97=8FElectro-Optical/Infrared (EO/IR) technology integrates two powe=
rful imaging methods into one system.</p>

<p>=E2=97=8FElectro-Optical (EO): Functions like a high-definition camera, =
capturing images in the visible light spectrum to provide sharp detail and =
=E2=97=8Fobject recognition when lighting conditions are favorable.</p>

<p>=E2=97=8FInfrared (IR): Detects heat energy emitted by all objects, enab=
ling vision in total darkness and through smoke, haze, or rain by highlight=
ing temperature differences.</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p><span style=3D"font-size:32px"><strong>How EO/IR Systems Operate=EF=BC=
=9F</strong></span></p>

<p>=E2=97=8FSensing: EO sensors collect visual imagery while IR sensors det=
ect thermal radiation.</p>

<p>=E2=97=8FIntegration: The system merges both data streams, combining vis=
ible details with heat signatures.</p>

<p>=E2=97=8FOutput: Operators receive a unified, real-time image, deliverin=
g actionable insights in critical environments.</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p><span style=3D"font-size:32px"><strong>Key Benefits</strong></span></p>

<p>=E2=97=8F24/7 Monitoring: Effective in both daylight and complete darkne=
ss.</p>

<p>=E2=97=8FWeather Resilience: IR capability ensures visibility through ch=
allenging conditions such as fog, rain, or smoke.</p>

<p>=E2=97=8FComprehensive Awareness: Reveals both physical details and hidd=
en thermal activity.</p>

<p>=E2=97=8FHigh Precision: Supports accurate detection, recognition, and t=
racking of targets.</p>

<p><br>
<span style=3D"font-size:32px"><strong>Typical Applications</strong></span>=
</p>

<p>=E2=97=8FDefense &amp; Security: Surveillance, reconnaissance, and targe=
t tracking for military and border protection.</p>

<p>=E2=97=8FPublic Safety: Essential for firefighting, search-and-rescue mi=
ssions, and disaster response.</p>

<p>=E2=97=8FIndustrial Use: Powerline inspections, pipeline monitoring, and=
 predictive maintenance.</p>

<p>=E2=97=8FCommercial Sector: Enhancing maritime patrol, aviation safety, =
and advanced driver-assistance systems</p>

<p><br>
&nbsp;</p>

<p><span style=3D"font-size:32px"><strong>FAQ</strong></span></p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p><strong>1. What is an EO/IR system and how does it work?</strong><br>
An EO/IR system combines Electro-Optical (EO) sensors and Infrared (IR) sen=
sors. The EO sensor captures high-resolution imagery in visible light, whil=
e the IR sensor detects thermal radiation emitted by objects. Together, the=
y provide clear visuals in both day and night conditions, as well as throug=
h obscurants like fog, smoke, or rain.</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p><strong>2. What are the main applications of EO/IR systems?</strong><br>
EO/IR systems are widely used for surveillance, reconnaissance, border secu=
rity, search and rescue, maritime monitoring, and drone operations. They al=
low operators to detect, identify, and track targets in various environment=
s and lighting conditions.</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p><strong>3. What is the range and resolution of EO/IR systems?</strong><b=
r>
The range and resolution vary by model. Typically, high-end EO/IR systems c=
an detect human-sized targets at several kilometers and provide HD imagery.=
 Many systems also support zoom and tracking functions for precise identifi=
cation.</p>

<p><br>
<strong>4. Can EO/IR systems operate in complete darkness or adverse weathe=
r?</strong><br>
Yes. The infrared component allows the system to detect thermal signatures =
in total darkness, smoke, fog, or light rain. However, heavy precipitation =
or extreme weather may slightly reduce detection performance.</p>

<p><br>
<strong>5. How is the EO/IR system mounted or integrated?</strong><br>
EO/IR systems can be mounted on drones, vehicles, ships, or stationary plat=
forms. Many systems feature gimbals for 360=C2=B0 rotation, stabilization, =
and automatic target tracking, ensuring clear imagery even on moving platfo=
rms.</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p><strong>6. What maintenance or operational support is required for EO/IR=
 systems?</strong><br>
Regular cleaning of lenses, firmware updates, and periodic calibration are =
recommended. Most modern EO/IR systems are designed for low-maintenance ope=
ration and come with technical support and training from the manufacturer<b=
r>
